! H2O | Standalone water at wB97X-D/6-21G+(d,p)/PCM(water)
!
! Part of the standalone hydration thermodynamic cycle for acetaldehyde:
!   dG_hydration = G(hydrate) - [G(aldehyde) + G(water)]
! See aa002-aldehyde-bare.inp for full provenance notes on the literature
! comparison (Sorensen & Jencks, JACS 1987, K_h = 1.2 +/- 0.1).
!
! Kept at the SAME level of theory as the rest of the aa001 series
! (wB97X-D/6-21G+(d,p)/PCM(water)) for consistency.
!
! Starting geometry: one of the genuinely intact spectator water
! molecules (O8/H9/H13, both hydrogens confirmed by direct O-H distance
! checks: 0.961 A and 0.981 A) extracted from the converged aa001h
! (aldehyde) cluster geometry, purely as a reasonable starting guess --
! it will fully relax on optimization regardless. NZVAR=3 (3*3-6) for
! this 3-atom system.
!
! NOTE (correction): the first version of this file incorrectly used
! O8/H9/H10 -- H10 is actually covalently bonded to O7 (0.981 A), not
! O8 (1.769 A, a hydrogen-bond distance, not a real O-H bond). This was
! only checked via C3-O distances earlier (confirming neither water was
! bonded to carbon), not each water's own internal O-H pairing. GAMESS's
! automatic internal-coordinate generation correctly caught this --
! "THERE ARE NOT ENOUGH PRIMITIVE INTERNAL COORDINATES" -- since the
! genuine bond count for this "molecule" was only 1, not 2.

 $BASIS GBASIS=N21 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1 NPFUNC=1 DIFFSP=.t. $END
 $CONTRL SCFTYP=RHF RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE NZVAR=3 $END
 $CONTRL DFTTYP=wB97X-D $END
 $SCF DIIS=.t. DAMP=.t. $END
 $STATPT OPTTOL=0.00005 NSTEP=200 IHREP=20 HSSEND=.t. $END
 $ZMAT DLC=.t. AUTO=.t. $END
 $FORCE METHOD=SEMINUM PURIFY=.t. $END
 $PCM SOLVNT=WATER $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=20 MEMDDI=20 $END
!$CONTRL EXETYP=CHECK $END

 $DATA
Water, standalone, for acetaldehyde hydration thermodynamic cycle
C1
O     8.0      3.5486492584     2.8311475219    -4.6311803360
H     1.0      3.0765449397     3.5122781864    -5.1178290703
H     1.0      3.2539156984     2.8458984372    -3.6954621779
 $END
